#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# asymptotic_product

#% text
# `asymptotic_product(f, [k, a, b], [x, x0, m])` gives the expansion of the closed-form product of f over k to order m in x at x0; `x -> x0` gives the leading term.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
asymptotic_product(1 + a/k^2, [k, 1, 3], [a, 0, 2])
#% output
#= 1 + (49/36)*a + (7/18)*a^2

#% cell
asymptotic_product(k + m, [k, 1, 4], [m, 0, 1])
#% output
#= 24 + 50*m

#% cell
asymptotic_product((k + 1)/k, [k, 1, n], [n, 2, 1])
#% output
#= 1 + n

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `product`, `series`, `asymptotic_sum`
